# A `<` hint that makes an empty rule win over shifting builds a table that
# pushes forever on "x" (the generated parser hung on "xc"); rejected.
# error: empty_reduction_loop.grammar:19:1:
# error: reducing the empty rule b on X leads back to the same state
@lexer
tokens
    x
    c
    eof
    err
'x'   → x
'c'   → c
.     → err

@parser
top! = a
a = b a C → (a 2)
  | X
b = <
